\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the feature extraction and score generation pipeline. Phage genomes are translated into proteins and encoded using protein language model embeddings. The EMPATHI pipeline assigns functional categories, which are evaluated across $M = 2{,}160$ host function base classifiers ($M_{h,k}$). Finally, $\text  {NaN}$ aware mean pooling aggregates protein predictions into a $K_{\text  {tot}} = 2{,}036$-dimensional phage level score vector.\relax }}{30}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:data_generation_pipeline}{{\M@TitleReference {4.1}{Overview of the feature extraction and score generation pipeline. Phage genomes are translated into proteins and encoded using protein language model embeddings. The EMPATHI pipeline assigns functional categories, which are evaluated across $M = 2{,}160$ host function base classifiers ($M_{h,k}$). Finally, $\text  {NaN}$ aware mean pooling aggregates protein predictions into a $K_{\text  {tot}} = 2{,}036$-dimensional phage level score vector.\relax }}{30}{Overview of the feature extraction and score generation pipeline. Phage genomes are translated into proteins and encoded using protein language model embeddings. The EMPATHI pipeline assigns functional categories, which are evaluated across $M = 2{,}160$ host function base classifiers ($M_{h,k}$). Finally, $\text {NaN}$ aware mean pooling aggregates protein predictions into a $K_{\text {tot}} = 2{,}036$-dimensional phage level score vector.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
